  "illustration_prompt": "Create a single publication-quality landscape 3:2 narrative illustration for an adult illustrated English-reading booklet. Finished standalone artwork, not a book mockup, not a collage of multiple unrelated panels. Sophisticated contemporary editorial gouache and watercolor, carefully controlled colored-pencil accents, velvety matte paint, subtle warm paper texture, soft natural daylight. Warm ivory paper dominates; subdued eucalyptus and sage greens structure the composition; restrained buttery lemon-yellow and dusty terracotta accents. Calm, comfortable, refined, credible drawing and natural anatomy. An airy coherent composition with one clear story focal point and at most two supporting details, generous breathing room at all edges and softly feathered painted edges into ivory. Detailed but uncluttered. Historically and scientifically appropriate objects, clothing and setting. Show the particular article's pivotal event or mechanism rather than a generic portrait or generic textbook symbols. Human figures treated with dignity; no grotesque caricature, no sensational violence or visible injuries. For disasters, emphasize the setting, evidence or human response without graphic suffering. For uncertain scientific claims, depict the observations and investigation without presenting debated mechanisms as proven. Absolutely no typography, captions, letters, numbers, logos, watermarks, diagram labels, fake writing or invented charts anywhere. Do not render invisible forces as literal magic. Avoid corporate vector icons, slick 3D rendering and childish cartoon style. High-quality, print-ready visual storytelling, matching a warm ivory-and-sage adult watercolor booklet.\n\nARTICLE66: A single elegant tabletop observation explaining the burr-inspired hook-and-loop fastener. Main focal object is one real small dried burdock seed-head clinging to an unpatterned sage wool fabric swatch with clearly visible little loops. A natural adult hand holds a simple period hand magnifier above the attachment; through its glass a few physically plausible curved burr hooks catch fabric loops, without arrows or drawn labels. Supporting detail is a small pair of plain nylon hook-and-loop strips lying partially peeled apart on the same table, showing a practical material inspired by the plant. Keep botanical anatomy credible: roundish brown-green burdock burr with fine curved hooks, not a cactus, not sewing needles. No oversized fantasy seed, no floating microscope graphics, no NASA logos, patent text or brand names. Soft warm ivory paper, eucalyptus-green cloth, restrained ochre burr, quiet adult editorial gouache-watercolor.",
